{
  "$comment": [
    "Every sound the product ships, and where it came from.",
    "",
    "Read by tools/audio/fetch.mjs, which downloads, processes and writes",
    "frontend/public/audio/CREDITS.md from these rows. Adding a sound means adding",
    "a row here and re-running the sync — nothing is ever dropped into",
    "frontend/public/audio by hand, or the credits stop being true.",
    "",
    "Licences: 'pixabay' rows are the Pixabay Content License (free for commercial",
    "use, no attribution required); 'freesound' rows are CC0 and nothing else — the",
    "search in fetch.mjs cannot return anything but CC0, and that is deliberate.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  id        what the code asks for (frontend/src/lib/audio/library.ts)",
    "  group     for `sync <group>`, and for how the runtime loads it",
    "  file      relative to frontend/public/audio",
    "  shape     oneshot | loop | track — see the three make* functions",
    "  start     seconds into the source to begin. Skips intros, settling, and",
    "            whatever the recordist did before they stopped moving",
    "  duration  seconds to take",
    "  peakDb    one-shots: what the loudest sample is normalised to. The mix",
    "            table in AudioBus assumes every one-shot is the same distance",
    "            from full scale, so this is how a chirp and a knock stay",
    "            comparable. Quieter numbers for things that should sit back",
    "  lufs      long-form: integrated loudness to match to",
    "  crossfade loops: seconds of overlap at the seam"
  ],

